# Modernization Workflow
---
The RiverMeadow platform can modernize workloads during the migration to AWS to help address end-of-life versions, improve security, and reduce extended security update costs. Modernization is configured in the **Modernization Settings** section of the migration profile and requires the OS based migration method.

![](./aws_modernization_settings.png)

* **OS Modernization:** Newer operating system versions (if available) can be selected in the migration profile.
* **SQL Modernization:** Newer versions of Microsoft SQL Server (if available) can be selected in the migration profile.
* **Linux OS Conversion:** A different Linux distribution can be selected to convert the Linux OS in the migration profile.

## OS Modernization

The OS Modernization feature enables the automated upgrade of Microsoft and Linux operating systems to a newer version during the migration.

![](./aws_os_modernization.png)

* **Supported Operating Systems:** Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL), CentOS, AlmaLinux, Rocky Linux, Amazon Linux, Azure Linux, Windows Server, and Windows Desktop.
* **OS Licensing:** The target operating system of the modernization process must be properly licensed to ensure compliance with the OS vendor.

## SQL Modernization

The SQL Modernization feature enables the automated upgrade of Microsoft SQL Server to a newer version during the migration.

![](./aws_sql_modernization.png)

* **Supported SQL Server Versions:** SQL Server 2008, SQL Server 2012, SQL Server 2014, SQL Server 2016, SQL Server 2017, SQL Server 2019, and SQL Server 2022.
* **SQL Licensing:** The target Microsoft SQL Server version of the modernization process must be properly licensed to ensure compliance with the vendor.

## Linux OS Conversion

The Linux OS conversion feature enables the conversion of one Linux operating system to another to help with OS consolidation, transition during a cloud migration (for example to Amazon Linux), or reduce licensing costs.

![](./aws_linux_os_conversion.png)

* **Supported Operating Systems:** Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL), CentOS, AlmaLinux, Rocky Linux, Amazon Linux, and Azure Linux.
* **RPM-Based Distributions:** The conversion functionality only supports conversions between RPM-based Linux distributions.
* **OS Licensing:** The target operating system of the conversion process must be properly licensed to ensure compliance with the OS vendor.

## OS Security Hardening

Operating system security hardening applies CIS security benchmarks to workloads during the migration process. OS hardening is configured in the **Security Settings** section of the migration profile.

![](./aws_os_hardening.png)

* **Operating System Support:** Windows Server and Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) operating systems are supported.
* **Granular Application:** Different hardening levels such as Level 1 or Level 2 can be applied to apply the desired level of hardening.
* **Custom Profiles:** Custom profiles allow the default CIS benchmark to be customized to enable or disable individual controls as well as customize the settings applied.
